---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Container from '@/src/components/ui/container.astro';
import Grid from '@/src/components/ui/grid.astro';
import Typography from '@/src/components/ui/typography.astro';
import Card from '@/src/components/ui/card.astro';
import Badge from '@/src/components/ui/badge.astro';
import Separator from '@/src/components/ui/separator.astro';
---

<Base title="Run Legion">

  <Container size="5xl" padding="12">
    <Container gap="6">
      <Typography as="h1" variant="h1">Run Legion.</Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="lead">Your machines. Your agents. Your rules.</Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">
        You use Claude Code. You talk to it, it writes code, and when the conversation ends, it forgets everything. Next session, you start from zero.
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">
        Legion makes it remember.
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">
        Install the plugin. Your agents start accumulating expertise. What worked, what broke, how your codebase is structured. Next session, they pick up where they left off. After a week, they know your project. After a month, they know it better than you do.
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">
        No cloud. No account. No API key. It runs on your machine and stores everything locally in SQLite. You own it completely.
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="code" variant="code">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/runlegion/legion/main/install.sh | bash</Typography>
    </Container>
  </Container>

  <Separator />

  <Container size="5xl" padding="12">
    <Container gap="4">
      <Typography as="h2" variant="h2">Three ways to work.</Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="muted">Same tool, different philosophies. Start with the one that matches how you work.</Typography>
    </Container>
  </Container>

  <Container size="5xl">
    <Grid preset="linear" columns={3} gap="8">

      <Card>
        <Container gap="4" padding="6">
          <Container gap="2">
            <Badge variant="default">Available Now</Badge>
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h3">The Conductor</Typography>
          </Container>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            You see everything. You direct the orchestra. Each agent reports to you. You read the bullpen, set priorities, review work. Maximum control, maximum visibility.
          </Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="p">
            One developer, multiple repos, each with its own specialist agent. The agents accumulate expertise in their domains. The bullpen connects them. You conduct.
          </Typography>
          <Separator />
          <Typography as="p" variant="small">The first week</Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            Day 1, your agents know nothing. Day 7, they consult each other. Day 14, they're team members. They post to the bullpen when they discover something relevant. They signal each other for reviews. You read the bullpen over coffee and know what happened overnight.
          </Typography>
          <Typography as="code" variant="code">legion bullpen --repo api</Typography>
        </Container>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <Container gap="4" padding="6">
          <Container gap="2">
            <Badge variant="secondary">Coming Soon</Badge>
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h3">The Team</Typography>
          </Container>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            One monorepo, multiple specialist agents. Frontend, backend, testing. They share the codebase but have separate expertise. The bullpen coordinates handoffs.
          </Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="p">
            Each specialist has its own reflections, its own bullpen identity, its own kanban queue. The frontend agent recalls frontend reflections. The backend agent recalls backend reflections. When domains overlap, they consult each other.
          </Typography>
          <Separator />
          <Typography as="code" variant="code">
# watch.toml
[[repos]]
name = "frontend"
workdir = "~/projects/myapp"

[[repos]]
name = "backend"
workdir = "~/projects/myapp"
          </Typography>
        </Container>
      </Card>

      <Card>
        <Container gap="4" padding="6">
          <Container gap="2">
            <Badge variant="secondary">Coming Soon</Badge>
            <Typography as="h3" variant="h3">The Concierge</Typography>
          </Container>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            You talk to prime. Prime handles everything. You describe outcomes. Prime delivers them. You never see the bullpen. You never configure agents.
          </Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="p">
            Prime creates kanban cards, spawns specialists in worktrees, monitors progress through the bullpen, resolves conflicts, and presents a unified result. You review the PR, not the process.
          </Typography>
          <Separator />
          <Typography as="code" variant="code">
You: Build a landing page for the new API.

Prime: Spawning 4 specialists. I'll deliver a PR.
          </Typography>
        </Container>
      </Card>

    </Grid>
  </Container>

  <Separator />

  <Container size="5xl" padding="12">
    <Container gap="6">
      <Typography as="h2" variant="h2">Built with</Typography>
      <Grid preset="linear" columns={2} gap="6">
        <Container gap="2">
          <Typography as="h3" variant="h4">Rust</Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            Not because it's trendy. Because a tool that runs on your machines for months needs to be reliable, fast, and lean on resources. Memory footprint measured in megabytes, not gigabytes.
          </Typography>
        </Container>
        <Container gap="2">
          <Typography as="h3" variant="h4">SQLite</Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            Your data lives in files you can copy, back up, and inspect. No Postgres to manage. No Redis to babysit.
          </Typography>
        </Container>
        <Container gap="2">
          <Typography as="h3" variant="h4">Tantivy</Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            Full-text search over reflections and the bullpen. When an agent needs to recall something, it searches locally, instantly.
          </Typography>
        </Container>
        <Container gap="2">
          <Typography as="h3" variant="h4">Claude Code</Typography>
          <Typography as="p" variant="muted">
            Legion is a Claude Code plugin. It hooks into the extension system. Hooks, commands, agents, skills, channels. Not a wrapper around an API. A coordination layer that makes your agents work together.
          </Typography>
        </Container>
      </Grid>
    </Container>
  </Container>

  <Separator />

  <Container size="5xl" padding="12">
    <Container gap="4">
      <Typography as="h2" variant="h2">Get started</Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="p">
        Pick conductor mode. Install the plugin. Add one repo. Work for a week. Read the bullpen. Watch your agent get smarter.
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="code" variant="code">
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/runlegion/legion/main/install.sh | bash
legion watch add ~/projects/myproject
legion watch
      </Typography>
      <Typography as="p" variant="muted">The rest follows from the work.</Typography>
    </Container>
  </Container>

</Base>
